The one place a code signature really evaluates trust says what it got.

The signing certificate's own chain is deliberately NOT evaluated during a code-signature check:
the caller asks for the SecTrust by copy, and the smime library only evaluates when it is not asked
for one. So a certificate status of 0 further up never meant a chain had been checked. The TIMESTAMP
is the first thing that really asks, which is why it is the first to fail, and this line is what
made that visible:

    CIDER_TSA SecTrustEvaluate result=0 trustResult=0 cssmResultCode=0 (getCssm=0)

trustResult 0 is kSecTrustResultInvalid, the case Apple own code marks "should never happen". It
happens because SecTrustEvaluateIfNecessary cannot reach trustd, and its ramdisk fallback then
returns SUCCESS while leaving the result Invalid.

--- a/OSX/libsecurity_smime/lib/tsaSupport.c
+++ b/OSX/libsecurity_smime/lib/tsaSupport.c
@@ -1068,6 +1068,26 @@
         result = SecTrustEvaluate (trustRef, &trustResultType);
         dtprintf("[%s] SecTrustEvaluate: result: %d, trustResult: %s (%d)\n",
             __FUNCTION__, result, trustResultTypeString(trustResultType), trustResultType);
+        {
+            /*
+             * THE ONLY PLACE A CODE SIGNATURE ACTUALLY EVALUATES TRUST. The signing certificate's
+             * own chain is deliberately NOT evaluated here (the caller asks for the SecTrust by
+             * copy, and the smime library only evaluates when it is not asked for one), so a
+             * certificate status of 0 further up never meant a chain had been checked. The
+             * timestamp is the first thing that really asks, which is why it is the first to fail.
+             */
+            const char *cider = getenv("CIDER_TRACE_SECITEM");
+
+            if (cider != NULL && cider[0] != '\0') {
+                OSStatus cssm = 0;
+                OSStatus got = SecTrustGetCssmResultCode(trustRef, &cssm);
+
+                fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_TSA SecTrustEvaluate result=%d trustResult=%d "
+                        "cssmResultCode=%d (getCssm=%d)\n",
+                        (int) result, (int) trustResultType, (int) cssm, (int) got);
+                fflush(stderr);
+            }
+        }
         if (result)
             goto xit;
         switch (trustResultType)
